# AssignInstantActions — request the master to dispatch a VDA5050
# InstantActions message to one AGV, gated by the synchronous
# instant-action validator chain (action conflict detection §6.12,
# operating-mode gate §6.10.6 with §6.8.1 allowlist exemption,
# duplicate action_id detection §6.6.2). Wraps
# VDA5050Master::assign_instant_actions. Service half of Task #61.
#
# This is the GENERIC entry point for ALL instant actions — predefined
# (cancelOrder, startPause, stopPause, stateRequest, factsheetRequest,
# logReport, initPosition, startCharging, stopCharging) and custom
# (any actionType the AGV factsheet declares). FMS clients build the
# desired Action(s) into an InstantActions message and send via this
# service; the master routes them via MQTT to the AGV's instantActions
# topic at QoS 0 (§6.9).
#
# Compared to AssignOrder:
#   - InstantActions are NOT subject to graph / traversability /
#     stitching validation. They go through schema (#23) + PreSend
#     (#16) + action conflict detection (#22) + the §6.10.6 mode gate.
#   - The C++ entry point is `master.assign_instant_actions(...)` —
#     parallel to `master.assign_order(...)` from #15.
#
# **`ASSIGNED` semantics**: pre-flight passed; the InstantActions
# message has been queued for publish on the master's queue-processor
# thread. NOT AGV-acknowledged. Per §6.6.2, the AGV will report
# action_state.action_status transitions (WAITING → INITIALIZING →
# RUNNING → FINISHED / FAILED) on its State topic — FMS observes
# action progress via the OrderStatus topic's `action_states[]` field.
#
# **Idempotency**: each Action carries a unique `action_id` (UUID
# recommended, §6.6.2). Re-sending the same `action_id` is rejected
# as DUPLICATE_ACTION_ID. FMS owns action_id uniqueness.
#
# **Cancellation**: an in-flight instant action is cancelled by
# sending a `cancelOrder` instant action (which cancels the active
# order AND its associated action_states). There is no per-action
# cancel.

# Required: AGV identity. Empty values are rejected as INVALID_REQUEST.
string manufacturer
string serial_number

# The instant actions to dispatch. May contain 1+ actions. Each
# action.action_id must be globally unique (UUID recommended); the
# master rejects DUPLICATE_ACTION_ID against the active order's
# action_ids and against in-flight action_states[].
vda5050_interfaces/InstantActions instant_actions
---
# Decision enum — values 0–7 mirror C++ InstantActionDecision
# (instant_action_assignment_result.hpp) one-to-one. Value 8
# (INVALID_REQUEST) is service-only: empty manufacturer or
# serial_number, rejected before reaching the C++ entry point.
# Sequential — future codes appended.
#
# ASSIGNED                       — pre-flight passed; actions queued for publish
#                                  (NOT AGV-acknowledged — see header).
# AGV_NOT_ONBOARDED              — no AGV with this {manufacturer, serial_number}.
# AGV_OFFLINE                    — connection_state != ONLINE; QoS 0 send to
#                                  offline AGV is silently dropped, so we reject.
# DUPLICATE_ACTION_ID            — one or more candidate action_ids collide
#                                  within the batch, with active in-flight
#                                  actions, or with the active order.
#                                  Empty action_id also rejected here.
# AGV_QUEUE_FULL                 — AGV's outbound queue is full; FMS dispatching
#                                  faster than AGV processes.
# HARD_ACTION_BLOCKED            — HARD-blocking candidate while AGV has at
#                                  least one in-flight action (§6.12).
# ACTION_BLOCKED_BY_DRIVING      — SOFT- or HARD-blocking candidate while AGV
#                                  is driving (§6.12).
# AGV_MODE_NOT_AUTO_FOR_ACTION   — AGV not in AUTOMATIC/SEMIAUTOMATIC AND the
#                                  candidate action_type is not on the §6.8.1
#                                  instant-scope allowlist.
# INVALID_REQUEST                — service-level: empty manufacturer or
#                                  serial_number in the request.
uint8 ASSIGNED=0
uint8 AGV_NOT_ONBOARDED=1
uint8 AGV_OFFLINE=2
uint8 DUPLICATE_ACTION_ID=3
uint8 AGV_QUEUE_FULL=4
uint8 HARD_ACTION_BLOCKED=5
uint8 ACTION_BLOCKED_BY_DRIVING=6
uint8 AGV_MODE_NOT_AUTO_FOR_ACTION=7
uint8 INVALID_REQUEST=8
uint8 decision

# Echo of {manufacturer, serial_number} for FMS-side correlation when
# fanning out N async calls. action_ids are inside the request's
# instant_actions msg — FMS already has them.
string manufacturer
string serial_number

# Diagnostic errors populated for non-ASSIGNED decisions. Empty on
# success. Same content as InstantActionAssignmentResult.errors,
# converted via the existing to_msg<> template.
vda5050_interfaces/Error[] errors
